# Drafted by Gemini (R20), edited. R20 side quest: The Quiet Door. Marianna Grey is hiding Mrs. Oakum from the mob; the party escorts her to the estate in three legs.

~ start
Narrator: Marianna Grey stands pressed against the rough timber at the corner of the stable yard, her face pale in the gloom. She beckons to you with a cold, trembling hand, not making a sound.
interject name:silas_vane: Someone's about to ask for a very pricey favour. I can smell it.
marianna_grey [afraid]: I have Mrs. Oakum hidden up in the loft above the stalls. The mob has her name now. I need to get her out of Wickermoor, and I didn't know who else to ask.
* We will take her up to the estate. -> accept
* Why does the mob want Mrs. Oakum? -> why
* We cannot help her right now. -> refuse

~ why
marianna_grey [sad]: She is a good woman, truly, though she walks out alone when the moon is high. Tonight, with the village in this fever, the mob won't need more reason than that.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Nocturnal wandering is hardly a pathology worth bringing out the pitchforks, darling.
-> start
~ refuse
approve tobin_hayward -2 silas_vane -2 lucan_houndstooth -1: You refused to help Marianna hide Mrs. Oakum from the mob
marianna_grey [sad]: Oh. Yes, I understand. It is a terrible night to ask so much of anyone.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Leaving good stock to the fire when a hand could save it. Shameful.
-> END
~ accept
approve tobin_hayward +2 silas_vane +2 rook_coldwake +2: You agreed to smuggle Mrs. Oakum away from the mob
set rk_quiet_asked
quest quiet_door asked
marianna_grey [smile]: Thank you, truly. She is up in the hayloft right now. Go in by the side door and keep low.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Up in the dry straw, then. Keep your lanterns shuttered on the ladder.
-> END

~ progress
if flag.rk_oakum_gone
marianna_grey [weary]: The stable is quiet again now. Thank you for what you did.
-> END
endif
Narrator: Marianna's wide eyes flick toward the latched stable door and right back to you, the smell of damp straw and nervous horses thick in the air.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The horses have caught the crowd's scent on the wind. Quietly now.
marianna_grey [afraid]: Mrs. Oakum is still waiting up in the loft. Please, you must hurry before the torches come back down this lane.
-> END

~ oakum
Narrator: Mrs. Oakum sits among the scratchy hay bales, a big woman folded small in the dark. She holds an iron pitchfork across her knees that you can tell she has no intention of using.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Observe her grip on the iron, friends; she fears her own teeth.
mrs_oakum [afraid]: I don't want to hurt a living soul, truly I don't. But if that crowd corners me in the dark, I might lose hold of myself, and I'd never forgive that.
* Come on, we are leading you out now. -> lead_out
* Stay quiet and wait here a little longer. -> END

~ lead_out
approve rook_coldwake +2 tobin_hayward +2 lucan_houndstooth +1: You led Mrs. Oakum out of the stable to safety
set rk_oakum_escort
Narrator: Mrs. Oakum props the pitchfork against a bale and follows you down the loft ladder, out through the back of the stable.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Single file by the timber. Keep your boots quiet.
move wickermoor_village:from_stable

~ leg1
Narrator: The lane behind the stalls offers forty yards of deep shadow before the Founder's Round. Beyond the split-rail fence, pitch torches hiss and bob in the night wind.
* [Stealth DC 15] Creep along the wall in the shadow. -> leg2 | spotted
* [Deception DC 14] Cover her in a sack and claim she is a butcher's pig. -> leg2 | spotted
* Take Marianna's mare and cart the long way by the river. -> leg2_long

~ leg2_long
approve tobin_hayward +2 rook_coldwake +1 delphine_ravelle -1: You took the slow, safe river road with Marianna's mare
time +120
Narrator: The old mare plods slow and steady beside the wet, rushing hush of the river. Nobody looks twice at a heavy woman riding a cart of sweet hay.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Hay-cart billing in the dark, darlings. Wait till my public hears of this.
-> leg2

~ leg2
Narrator: You reach the edge of the Founder's Round, where the press of bodies is thickest. Acrid smoke drifts beneath the great Oak, its crooked boughs lit orange from below.
* [Stealth DC 15] Slip along the dark shadow of the buildings. -> leg3 | spotted
* [Performance DC 14] Stumble through like drunks singing the mob's chant. -> leg3 | spotted
* Hide in the dark and wait an hour for them to scatter. -> leg3_wait

~ leg3_wait
approve lucan_houndstooth +2 rook_coldwake +1 delphine_ravelle -2: You waited in the dark until the angry torches scattered
time +60
Narrator: The torches finally bob away down a crooked side lane, taking their angry muttering with them. For a brief, breathless stretch, the cobblestones of the Round lie empty.
interject name:silas_vane: House cleared the table for us, friend. Best move before they deal again.
-> leg3

~ leg3
Narrator: Ahead lies the open moor road and the long, steep climb through the mist. At the crest of the hill, the tall iron gates of the crooked estate wait against the sky.
* [Survival DC 12] Take the back path through the tangled heather. -> arrive | spotted
* Walk straight up the open road together. -> arrive

~ spotted
Narrator: A blazing pitch torch swings round, throwing harsh light across your faces. A hundred lilac-tinted eyes lock onto you, and a hundred throats take up the chant for Mrs. Oakum's blood.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Well, the house lights are up, darlings, and the cheap seats want blood.
mrs_oakum [afraid]: Leave me here, please. I can hold them off long enough for the rest of you to run.
* Draw steel and fight the mob off. -> fight_for_her
* [ends:quiet_door] Hand her over, we cannot win this. -> give_up

~ fight_for_her
approve rook_coldwake +3 lucan_houndstooth +3 silas_vane +2: You stood your ground and defended Mrs. Oakum from the mob
set rk_mob_down = now
combat rk_mob_fight

~ give_up
approve silas_vane -5 rook_coldwake -4 tobin_hayward -4: You handed Mrs. Oakum over to the waiting village mob
set rk_oakum_gone
set rk_oakum_taken
quest quiet_door taken
Narrator: The villagers take her arms with a strange, almost gentle care, and she does not look back as they lead her away. A heavy cell door clangs shut, and the whole lane goes quiet.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Look at their eyes, darling; so remarkably docile once the quarry yields.
-> END

~ arrive
set rk_oakum_gone
quest quiet_door delivered
Narrator: The crooked iron gates of the estate swing shut and swallow you in cool shadow. Beside you, Mrs. Oakum lets out a long, shaky breath she has been holding since supper.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Iron's latched and the road is clear. You're through, missus.
mrs_oakum [smile]: I reckon I owe you my life, and maybe theirs too. It is a mighty peculiar house up here, though it feels warm enough.
move druskenvald_estate:from_village

~ prisoner
Narrator: Mrs. Oakum sits on the cold stone bench in the end cell, her broad hands folded neatly in her lap, patient as a barn cow waiting out a storm.
mrs_oakum [weary]: Don't you fret none over me, I've weathered worse nights than this. The constable even brought me a wool blanket to keep the chill off.
-> END
